  "payload": {
    "commit": {
      "oid": "c48f531a3b9bea9d6f1d153b26bc5bcb0555ee9f",
      "authoredDate": "2026-07-28T18:39:28.000+02:00",
      "shortMessage": null,
      "shortMessageMarkdown": "<div>fix(reasoning): resolve effort in the runtime and stop offering rejected values</div>",
      "bodyMessageHtml": "Review pass over the APP-685 branch.\n\nBehavior:\n\n- The bundled effort is resolved in the agent runner instead of the chat TUI, so\n  evals, Slack, the API, and scheduled runs get it too. Previously only the TUI\n  applied it, which left the eval-consistency argument in the ticket unmet. A\n  command carrying any parameters keeps them verbatim; only a command with none\n  gets the default, so the TUI can send an empty `reasoning` for a model that\n  publishes no usable effort without the runtime refilling it.\n- The picker no longer falls back to the full enum when a model publishes a\n  supported-efforts list that decoded to nothing. That fallback put\n  provider-rejected values back in front of the user, which is the failure the\n  catalog lookup was added to prevent.\n- `reasoning.mandatory` is now read rather than merely decoded: `none` is not\n  offered for a model that cannot run with reasoning disabled.\n\nStructure:\n\n- Deleted `ChatOptions.parameters`, which no caller set, along with the merge\n  block duplicated across the invoke and spawn commands.\n- The effort enum is one tuple; the internal schema and every membership guard\n  derive from it. A hand-written `satisfies` list accepted a subset, so a new\n  level would have decode-failed at the boundary with typecheck green.\n- Broke the model-picker/use-model-picker import cycle, dropped a pass-through\n  hook, made `useModelPicker` take an options object, made `saveEffort`\n  required, and restored the picker comments the split had removed.\n\nVerified: bun run check, bun run typecheck, bun test (4245 pass; the 2 failures\nare pre-existing on the PR head - a sandbox process.execve limit and a local env\nkey). sentrux drops from 3 violations to 1, and that one predates this branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;",
